{"name":"World Peace","hex":"#005477","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"world peace","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The ideology of universal global understanding and non-violence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/world_peace"}],"entries":[{"title":"World peace","blocks":[{"text":"World peace is the concept of an ideal state of peace within and among all people and nations on Earth. Different cultures, religions, philosophies, and organizations have varying concepts on how such a state would come about."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Peace_symbol_%28fixed_width%29.svg/330px-Peace_symbol_%28fixed_width%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_peace"},{"title":"World Peace (sculpture)","blocks":[{"text":"World peace is a bronze sculpture donated by the city of Moscow, Russia to the city of Helsinki, Finland, created by sculptor Oleg Kiryuhin. The sculpture was located at Hakaniemenranta in Helsinki, and it was revealed on 14 January 1990, two months after the Berlin Wall had been broken. The sculpture belongs to the collection of the Helsinki Art Museum."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e3/Maailmanrauha.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Peace_(sculpture)"},{"title":"World","blocks":[{"text":"A world is a totality of entities. In philosophy, the world is customarily viewed as all of existence or the whole of reality. Some conceptions see the world as unique, while others examine the character of entities that exist in the world or talk of a plurality of worlds, challenging the idea that the world is an all-inclusive whole. The term is also commonly used as a context-dependent expression to denote a specific domain of discourse and everything within it, such as the Earth and all life on it or the whole of human existence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Hubble_ultra_deep_field.jpg/330px-Hubble_ultra_deep_field.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World"},{"title":"Peace","blocks":[{"text":"Peace is a state of harmony in the absence of hostility and violence. In a societal sense, peace is commonly used to mean a lack of conflict and freedom from fear of violence between individuals or groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg/330px-Peace_dove_%283329620077%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/The_Soviet_Union_1991_CPA_6375_stamp_%2813th_standard_issue_of_Soviet_Union._12th_issue._World_peace._Globe_and_palm_branch%29_1200dpi.jpg/500px-The_Soviet_Union_1991_CPA_6375_stamp_%2813th_standard_issue_of_Soviet_Union._12th_issue._World_peace._Globe_and_palm_branch%29_1200dpi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/The_Soviet_Union_1991_CPA_6375_stamp_%2813th_standard_issue_of_Soviet_Union._12th_issue._World_peace._Globe_and_palm_branch%29_1200dpi.jpg/500px-The_Soviet_Union_1991_CPA_6375_stamp_%2813th_standard_issue_of_Soviet_Union._12th_issue._World_peace._Globe_and_palm_branch%29_1200dpi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1984 USSR stamp illustrating the Earth behind a palm frond. The title reads: \"Мир Народам Земли!\" (\"Peace to all the Peoples of the World!\").","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Soviet_Union_1991_CPA_6375_stamp_(13th_standard_issue_of_Soviet_Union._12th_issue._World_peace._Globe_and_palm_branch)_1200dpi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Pattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_%28Page_1%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_%28Page_1%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Pattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_%28Page_1%29.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Pattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_%28Page_1%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Pattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_%28Page_1%29.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_%28Page_1%29.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Interfaith declaration on world peace from the 1941–43 bulletin for the Commission to Study the Organization of Peace","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APattern_For_Peace_Catholic%2C_Jewish_and_Protestant_Declaration_on_World_Peace_(Page_1).tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Statue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg/500px-Statue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Statue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg/1280px-Statue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Statue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg/500px-Statue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Statue of Buddha in the Darjeeling Peace Pagoda, India. This pagoda was designed by Japanese Buddhist monk Nichidatsu Fujii to unite people of all beliefs in their search for world peace.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStatue_of_Buddha_in_Japanese_Peace_Pagoda%2CDarjeeling.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mt._Ecclesia-3.jpg/500px-Mt._Ecclesia-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mt._Ecclesia-3.jpg/1280px-Mt._Ecclesia-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Mt._Ecclesia-3.jpg/500px-Mt._Ecclesia-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mount Ecclesia's long-standing suggestion for World Peace Meditation,[36] along with annual purposeful devotional dates,[37] as faithfully performed by its fraternal organization whose founder taught, in the 1910s, that \"Peace is a matter of education, and impossible of achievement until we have learned to deal charitably, justly, and openly with one another, as nations as well as individuals\"[38]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMt._Ecclesia-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Ranakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg/500px-Ranakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Ranakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg/1280px-Ranakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Ranakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg/500px-Ranakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Ranakpur Jain Temple, located in Ranakpur, India","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARanakpur_Jain_Temple_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/RUDN.jpg/500px-RUDN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/RUDN.jpg/1280px-RUDN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/RUDN.jpg/500px-RUDN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A copy of the sculpture on top of a pillar in front of the Peoples' Friendship University of Russia in Moscow.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARUDN.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/FontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg/500px-FontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/FontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg/1280px-FontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/FontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg/500px-FontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jean-Baptiste Carpeaux: Quatre parties du monde at the Jardin du Luxembourg in Paris.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFontaineQuatrePartiesDuMonde04.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Yggdrasil.jpg/500px-Yggdrasil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Yggdrasil.jpg/500px-Yggdrasil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yggdrasil, an attempt to reconstruct the Norse world tree wh